> 1. Some of my variables are of orders of magnitude larger than some others.

You can fix that by dividing by a constant that makes sense.  For example, dividing large-SD variables by 10 would allow you to interpret regression paths in terms of 10-unit changes instead of 1-unit changes.

SEMNET is a great forum for general SEM questions that are not software-specific:

http://www2.gsu.edu/~mkteer/semnet.html

