> Wild guess - does it have something to do with the equality of correlations between the other factors and both f5 and f7?

Yes, that's exactly it.  If those are the same variable, that implies their relationships with any other variable (e.g., with f1, with f2, etc.) would be identical.  Also, fixing the covariance to 1 only implies their correlation is 1 if the factors are standardized to have variances == 1.  You can do this with the argument std.lv <http://std.lv> = TRUE

